{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_49_1342244096#1_2785327046","relevance":3,"reason":"This is a dedicated PMI paper titled 'Project Manager as Team Coach - Plan for Success' that directly addresses how a project manager can coach effectively to improve team outcomes/performance, including what coaching is, why it matters for project teams, when and whom to coach, coaching methods, phases of engagement, and measuring success.","learned":"Project/team coaches can improve team outcomes by identifying coaching opportunities, using appropriate coaching methods, structuring coaching engagements in phases, and evaluating whether the coaching engagement succeeds."},"action":{"op":"next","qid":"q3378","reason":"This query surfaced a strong non-duplicate source on coaching to improve team outcomes, so continue the list for more directly relevant evidence."}}
{"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q3378"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_49_1342244096#2_2785329240","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q3378","rank":5,"snippet":"how to determine the success of the coaching engagement. Introduction Success in today’s business community requires a high level of effort to achieve <cover>goals that align with strategic organizational objectives. Many business leaders focus on professional development to ensure their continued successful performance. Leadership coaching is one method of improving performance, and anyone at any professional level can participate in a coaching relationship. Individuals can find coaches, and managers can coach their employees. As managers of project teams, project managers have a unique opportunity to increase the chance of successful project outcomes and increasing the performance of project team members at the same time. In this paper, we will look at the management activity of coaching and how a project manager can use coaching to improve project performance and project success. After defining coaching in terms of what it is and what it is not, the reasons for coaching will be presented.\" , \"start_char\": 1036.000000 , \"title\": \"Project Manager as Team Coach - </cover>Plan for Success\" , \"url\": \"https://www.pmi.org/learning/library/project-manager-team-coach-plan-success-6251\" }"}}
{"request":{"judgments":"15/50"}}
{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_49_1342244096#2_2785329240","relevance":3,"reason":"This is another directly relevant segment from the dedicated PMI paper 'Project Manager as Team Coach.' It states that leadership coaching improves performance and that project managers can use coaching to improve project performance, project success, and project team-member performance by aligning goals with organizational objectives and applying coaching relationships.","learned":"Team/project coaches improve performance by aligning team goals with strategic objectives, using leadership coaching relationships, and coaching team members to improve both project performance and project success."},"action":{"op":"next","qid":"q3378","reason":"The current query is yielding strong grade-3 evidence from a non-duplicate dedicated source, so continue to find additional actionable segments or sources."}}
{"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q3378"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_16_1461221183#1_1656176806","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q3378","rank":6,"snippet":"instructors, with input from the show's producers, while the choreography was done by Miller, her staff, and occasionally a guest choreographer. Various rival dance teams spurred the team's competitiveness. The show's success was often credited to the drama and conflict among Miller and the moms, along with the weekly dances and the close relationships among the girls as viewers watched them grow up and <cover>improve their skills. The show features Miller as an extremely strict dance team coach who, over the series, relied more and more on criticism, sometimes personal, to motivate the girls, with an emphasis on hard work and competition against teammates. Every week on the show, Miller used a pyramid of individual headshots and gave feedback to each girl about her ranking, previous week's performance, </cover>attitude, effort, and the behavior of the girl herself and her mother. Miller had never used a pyramid in her studio prior to Dance Moms, and when once asked about it, Miller stated, \"I've never done that in my life.\" , \"start_char\": 1325.000000 , \"title\": \"Dance Moms - Wikipedia\" , \"url\": \""}}
