{"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q3380"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_24_69343168#1_154683942","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q3380","rank":3,"snippet":"Great Examples of Candor Betty White Caroline Wanga Sir Patrick Stewart Why Candor Is Important Positive Communication Transparency Growth Mindset What Candor is NOT About Aggression Perfect Timing Personal Criticism Abilities That Lead To The Mastery of Candor Assuming the Best Intentions Being Considerate Being Objective Focusing on the Good of the Company Getting to the Point Sharing Specific Examples Staying Factual Who can benefit from practicing Candor? Explore Complementary Skills to Candor Body Language<cover>Coaching Leadership Gather feedback on over 30 skills from Matter. \" , \"segment\": \"When you exert candor in your communication, you encourage others to do the same. Candid communication allows you to both give and get the information you need to improve your team performance </cover>and professional growth. Matter’s Definition of Candor Communicates in a truthful and in a straightforward manner. Matter is based on an ontology of over 30 recommended skills. Great Examples of Candor Betty White The beloved actress of stage and screen, and former “Golden Girl,”is renowned for both her humor and her directness. In fact, they’re often so skillfully combined that it’s hard to tell them apart. She’s developed a reputation for “"}}
