{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_15_1828790213#0_3664195008","relevance":3,"reason":"This sports-coaching article is dedicated to trust as a factor in team success and directly supports how coaches can improve team performance: develop trust with players and among teammates, which strengthens cohesion, helps athletes and teams reach potential, maintains focus, and prevents performance declines caused by lack of trust.","learned":"Coaches can improve team performance by intentionally building trust within the team; trust supports cohesion, focus, confidence, athlete development, and reaching team potential."},"action":{"op":"next","qid":"q3382","reason":"The sports team-cohesion query is producing strong grade-3 evidence about actionable coaching mechanisms, so continue to find more relevant sources."}}
