{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_13_369606461#7_877791031","relevance":2,"reason":"The passage gives a relevant partial answer: managers can coach teams by observing individual and team performance, asking the right questions, providing feedback, and being approachable to improve outcomes. However, it is embedded in a hospitality training article rather than being dedicated to coaches improving team performance.","learned":"Manager-coaches can improve team outcomes by observing performance, asking questions, giving feedback, and shifting from a critical boss role to a supportive coach role."},"action":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"coach your team\" \"improve performance\")","reason":"Search for a more dedicated practical guide on coaching a team to improve performance, using the promising phrase from the latest result but removing hospitality-specific noise."}}
{"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"coach your team\" \"improve performance\")"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_40_1650845466#6_3359466409","ok":true,"op":"query","qid":"q3401","rank":1,"snippet":"a good manager is no longer good enough, consider this: Author (s) Get the insights you need to create an exceptional workplace. \" , \"segment\": \"New managers often feel like they ought to be the ones with all the answers. But asking for ideas to help solve problems and <cover>improve performance is actually a sign of manager confidence. In nearly every dimension of business success, the manager makes the difference. Only a third of U.S. employees strongly agree that their opinion at work seems to count. But when a manager takes an employee's opinion seriously and acts on it, that employee feels respected, connected and committed to the team. And, of course, a good idea improves outcomes for everyone else. Even if you can't make additional changes to a plan, hearing someone out is still valuable. 3. Coach your team </cover>in a way that allows for genuine candor. One manager described how they developed a culture of safety at his workplace:\" , \"start_char\": 2973.000000 , \"title\": \"8 Behaviors of the World's Best Managers\" , \"url\": \""}}
