{"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ coach trust \"team performance\" athletes)"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_44_1364749777#15_2865845666","ok":true,"op":"query","qid":"q3404","rank":1,"snippet":"Image On Your Site \" , \"segment\": \"You’re teaching them that there aren’t excuses, and anything is possible with hard work. 10) Learn to Be a Good Leader Coaches are leaders. While you have to learn to motivate and push your athletes, you have to learn to lead and inspire them too. To improve <cover>team performance, study greats like Abraham Lincoln, Martin Luther King Jr, Winston Churchill, or other leaders that personally inspire you. Learn the values that make a good leader, and work to exemplify them. You’ll be a role model for your athletes, and you’ll encourage them to be better people too. Also, make sure you don’t lose your team. They should have full confidence in you, as their coach. 11) Understand Limits To earn your player’s trust, </cover>you need to build a history of pushing them hard, but not harder than they can handle. Learn to understand your player’s limits and create a history that they can trust you.\" , \"start_char\": 6116.000000 , \"title\": \"14 Ways For Coaches To Improve Team Performance!\" ,"}}
{"request":{"judgments":"41/50"}}
{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_44_1364749777#15_2865845666","relevance":3,"reason":"This is a directly relevant segment from the dedicated article '14 Ways For Coaches To Improve Team Performance!' It explains that coaches improve team performance by learning to lead, motivate, inspire, model good leadership values, maintain team confidence, understand athletes' limits, and build player trust.","learned":"Coaches can improve team performance by being strong leaders and role models, motivating and inspiring athletes, earning trust, keeping team confidence, and pushing players without exceeding their limits."},"action":{"op":"next","qid":"q3404","reason":"The current trust/team-performance sports query produced a grade-3 result and may retrieve additional sources on trust as a mechanism for improving team performance, so continue briefly."}}
{"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q3404"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_44_1364749777#1_2865821138","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q3404","rank":2,"snippet":"want to see your athletes win and find the best part of themselves. You want to encourage strength, teamwork, and practice. You want to teach them perseverance. Whether you’re a new coach, or you’ve been coaching for 10 years or more, it never hurts to go back to the basics of being a good coach. There are a handful of things you can do to boost your team’s performance and help your <cover>athletes grow. 1) Focus on Your Relationship With Each Team Member Good coaches know that each member of the team is a vital part of the whole. Make sure you take the time to learn the individual strengths and weaknesses of each player and take time to build a relationship built on trust and encouragement. Your players need to know they can trust you as a coach, and when you push them, it’s to make them stronger.\" , \"start_char\": 290.000000 , \"title\": \"14 Ways For Coaches To Improve Team Performance!</cover>\" , \"url\": \"https://www.justfundraising.com/blog/14-ways-for-coaches-to-improve-team-performance/\" }"}}
